WEBVTT

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.800
Start in the admin

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.600
The Switch opens, with its tabs across the top

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.400
Add a brand starts with Step 0 · Check her

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.400
Steps 1 to 5 stay locked until the check passes — or until she's verified by hand

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.700
The Screen reads only free sources: her own pages, Wikipedia and SEC filings. About a third of a cent

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.700
Clicked into Her website

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.900
Typed a website that's already in The Switch

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:19.900
First it looks for her in The Switch — free

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.300
Already here: it stops, and nothing is spent. Open it takes you to that brand

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.600
Clicked into Her website

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.700
Typed a new brand's website

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.900
Not in The Switch yet — the Screen reads her site

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.100
Can't tell: her site names a founder, but nothing says who owns it today

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.800
Onboarding stays locked. Nothing is lost — it waits in Brand check

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.500
Six free checks. Each opens in your own browser: her About page, Google, certifications, Instagram, LinkedIn

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.000
This check cost a third of a cent. The full check, about seven cents, is only ever a button

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.900
Found the proof yourself? Say so here — it's logged with your name, the time and why

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.800
Chose what you relied on

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.000
Clicked into Where you saw it

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.400
A note alone isn't proof

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.700
Clicked into Your note

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.500
Typed a short note

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.300
The button stays off, and says why: a link or a named document is needed

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.300
Clicked into Where you saw it

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.200
Pasted the link to what you found

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.500
Now it can go

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.000
Logged — and onboarding opens

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.900
Step 0 shows how it opened. The other steps are open now

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.900
The date verified is still yours to set, in Owner and proof
